BT /F2 8 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 755.00 Tm (THE BIG MONEY PLAYBOOKS) Tj ET
0.6 w 54.00 747.00 m 558.00 747.00 l S
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 716.00 Tm (the regional manager's name and number, introduce yourself, and invite them to walk your facility and inspect your) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 700.77 Tm (equipment. In his words, it is 'very important to have the regional manager's name and number so you can introduce) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 685.55 Tm (yourself' [-0hAYhkhJaw @ 00:11:42]. He also works the field side by having adjusters and agents push for the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 670.32 Tm (company. That push lands hardest when claim volume is high and the program needs capacity [-0hAYhkhJaw @) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 655.10 Tm (00:12:01]. David Smith's addition is commitment. Once inside, learn both the program requirements and the carrier) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 639.87 Tm (requirements, because both rule sets apply to the same file [onSDIprTeAU @ 00:12:23]. The sequence matters.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 624.65 Tm (Applications sit dormant until a slot opens. The regional manager decides who fills that slot, and adjuster and agent) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 609.42 Tm (advocacy tips the decision. Whether a contractor stays on the list once the switch flips depends on mastering two) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 594.20 Tm (rulebooks.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 578.97 Tm (Inside the program, the drying math is dictated rather than negotiated. Schoen describes the 'micia' report, timestamped) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 563.75 Tm (day by day, which sets dehumidifier and air-mover counts that can fall below S500. If the room calls for a small dehu,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 548.52 Tm (you are paid for a small even if you placed a large [-0hAYhkhJaw @ 00:06:02]. David Smith sees contractors) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 533.30 Tm (overshoot in the other direction. They set '45 D HUs and 75 fans in two rooms' and then do not get paid for it) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 518.07 Tm ([onSDIprTeAU @ 00:44:40]. The paperwork load is a fixed cost to plan for. Documentation must be uploaded twice,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 502.85 Tm (once to your own system and once to the program, though some CRMs auto-upload [-0hAYhkhJaw @ 00:05:23].) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 487.62 Tm (Xactimate is mandatory and a second software platform may be required. Schoen tells owners to either train admin) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 472.40 Tm (staff or sub the paperwork out [-0hAYhkhJaw @ 00:06:42]. The practical read is direct. Set equipment to match what) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 457.17 Tm (the program's report will pay. Log readings daily to show specific humidity dropping, and keep estimating in Xactimate) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 441.95 Tm (from the first visit forward. Shops that set equipment by feel end up arguing with a reviewer over gear they already) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 426.72 Tm (paid to haul in, run and pull back out.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 411.50 Tm (The economics reward speed and volume rather than per-job margin. Schoen describes somewhat regular job flow) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 396.27 Tm (through rotation, scored on arrival speed and direct customer reviews. He is blunt that you are 'going to pay 5 10% a) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 381.05 Tm (fee to be on the program' [-0hAYhkhJaw @ 00:08:41]. He adds that mitigation pays well while construction is harder) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 365.82 Tm ([-0hAYhkhJaw @ 00:09:17]. The program wars show what TPAs actually sell to carriers. Alacrity won Nationwide by) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 350.60 Tm (promising $5M a year in savings, with no roughly $100 setup fee and no $150 service-call fee. Contractor Connection) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 335.37 Tm (took the account back with a 3-day drying cap it pitched as $20M in savings [-0hAYhkhJaw @ 00:03:50]. Each of) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 320.15 Tm (those savings is a line the contractor no longer bills. Ty Penzone explains how repair shops still make the channel) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 304.92 Tm (work: subs accept lower rates in exchange for year-round volume [onSDIprTeAU @ 00:55:23]. Put the numbers) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 289.70 Tm (together and the model is clear. Arrival speed and reviews win the rotation, and mitigation carries the margin while) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 274.47 Tm (construction fights the list. Every dollar a TPA promises a carrier comes out of fees and drying days the contractor used) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 259.25 Tm (to control. The model only works when crews and subs stay busy enough to spread the fee across many files.) Tj ET
