BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 493.77 Tm (Firsthand Failure Modes, Traps & Economics Checks) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 471.55 Tm (The most expensive trap is placing equipment the program will not pay for. Jon Schoen explains that the micia report is) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 456.32 Tm (timestamped day by day and dictates dehumidifier and air-mover counts, possibly below S500, so if the room calls for) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 441.10 Tm (a small dehu you are paid for a small even when you placed a large [-0hAYhkhJaw @ 00:06:02]. The caps come) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 425.87 Tm (straight from TPA sales pitches to carriers: Alacrity won Nationwide by promising $5M a year in savings by dropping) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 410.65 Tm (the roughly $100 setup fee and $150 service-call fee, and Contractor Connection won the account back with a three-day) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 395.42 Tm (drying cap claiming $20M in savings [-0hAYhkhJaw @ 00:03:50]. David Smith sees contractors set '45 D HUs and 75) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 380.20 Tm (fans in two rooms' and then get nothing for it [onSDIprTeAU @ 00:44:40]. Schoen's readings rule closes the loop: the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 364.97 Tm (logs must show specific humidity dropping day over day [-0hAYhkhJaw @ 00:08:21]. Even when the file is clean,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 349.75 Tm (Schoen warns payment is still not guaranteed, because a homeowner can walk away with the money. The economics) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 334.52 Tm (check is simple: run the job to the program's equipment math and drying window, not to your own habits, and log) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 319.30 Tm (readings that prove every day billed.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 304.07 Tm (The second trap is building a company whose survival depends on someone else's dispatch queue. Ty Penzone's) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 288.85 Tm (flooring company ran 125 homes a year from 2002 to 2006 while charging retail clients 1.5 times, then fell to one job) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 273.62 Tm (in a month in 2008 [onSDIprTeAU @ 00:56:46]. One DYOJO panelist puts it bluntly: 'I had a business that its entire) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 258.40 Tm (solvency was built around doing 150 jobs a year plus' [onSDIprTeAU @ 00:59:09], which is why Ty argues for) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 243.17 Tm (running diversified models to survive a 'model interrupt.' Back-office load is the quieter drain. Jon Schoen reports that) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 227.95 Tm (documentation must be uploaded twice unless a CRM auto-uploads, that Xactimate is mandatory and a second software) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 212.72 Tm (may be required, and that owners should plan to train admin staff or sub the paperwork out [-0hAYhkhJaw @) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 197.50 Tm (00:06:42]. Joe Boyle of ClearFile sees the same scheduling trap from the administrator's own licensing desk: approvals) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 182.27 Tm (take one week to three months, renewals cluster January through March, and financials must be current within 30 to 60) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 167.05 Tm (days, so step one is 'a very modest timeline' [kR0zavFV0HU @ 00:02:38]. Underestimating paperwork time, on either) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 151.82 Tm (side of the TPA relationship, quietly kills margin and deadlines.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 136.60 Tm (The third trap is signing or working under paper nobody read. On Relentless Health Value, 32BJ's Claire Brockbank) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 121.37 Tm (and host Stacey Richter peg about 95% of employers as deferring to the TPA's paper and losing rights in fine print like) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 106.15 Tm (a 'footnote on page 78,' because 'very few of us have contracting expertise, so we accept the language' [pNIYu-t990E @) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 90.92 Tm (00:06:09]. The cost was concrete: upside-down claims ran 32BJ about $10M in one year, with a $100 bill paid at $200,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 75.70 Tm (and the typical failure has sales overpromising, lawyers retracting, and contracting still open a year into implementation) Tj ET
